    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-07T10:49:19+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-07T10:49:19+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T00:19:19Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T00:19:19Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred well south of WA extends a ridge over northern and western SA. The high drifts over waters well to the south of SA over the weekend, while a developing low pressure system and trough in WA move close to the SA border. The high drifts southeast of Tasmania by Monday as the low moves across western SA on Monday and northern SA on Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-07T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-06T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, most likely in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds north of Marla in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 28 to 38.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending east to northeasterly in the early morning then increasing to 35 to 50 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers south of Woomera, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 34 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
